{"skill":{"slug":"runesleo-systematic-debugging","displayName":"Systematic Debugging"},"version":{"version":"3.0.0","createdAt":1772890916061,"changelog":"- Major update: Introduces a comprehensive four-phase (plus pre-phase) debugging process focused on root cause analysis before any fixes.\n- Adds a mandatory Phase 0: Context Recall—explicitly requires gathering prior knowledge and analyzing project context before investigating or proposing fixes.\n- Clearly defines strict phase order (Context Recall → Root Cause Investigation → Pattern Analysis → Hypothesis & Testing → Implementation) with rules to prevent skipping steps or guessing fixes.\n- Expands guidance for multi-component systems, systematic data/log gathering, and evidence-based analysis.\n- Includes red flags and common rationalizations to help users avoid pitfalls and maintain disciplined debugging.\n- Emphasizes test creation before fixing and sets hard limits on repeated failed fixes (triggers architectural review after three non-working attempts).","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9006,"sha256":"3ee7742b20dd0a2a935c46d65424cb8495b60020b8cad0fae3172933c05007bd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1739,"sha256":"6696ae06dc50f7c40678a67b357f26351dafd0989c3f630b5adf5444f7100c68","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789112194552,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"957e30bd4a8dbc88dc9feef328e738ca026a8c44608c9ddd14f66dc328ed3e27","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/957e30bd4a8dbc88dc9feef328e738ca026a8c44608c9ddd14f66dc328ed3e27","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085768824},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789112194552},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a normal debugging guide, but it directs agents to check memory files or past conversations before debugging, which can expose unrelated sensitive history.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Searching the current project, source code, tests, docs, and git history is proportionate for debugging; searching memory files or past conversations is overbroad without explicit scoping and user control.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill file with no bundled executable scripts, dependencies, remote fetches, or install-time behavior found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill makes context recall mandatory before all other work and has the agent summarize what it found, but does not require user consent, relevance limits, tenant/project boundaries, or redaction for memory or prior conversation content.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanism, service, hook, or privilege escalation is present. The phrase to record the solution later should be handled carefully so it does not write sensitive details into persistent memory without approval.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The root-cause debugging workflow is coherent with the stated purpose, but Phase 0 broadens it to prior memory files and past conversations, which is sensitive cross-session context not clearly needed for ordinary debugging.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing if your agent can access persistent memory, prior chats, or shared workspaces. It is not showing malware or exfiltration, but you should restrict context recall to the current project unless you explicitly approve broader memory or conversation access.","findings":"[T05] unexpected: The artifact-backed concern is the Phase 0 instruction to check MEMORY files or past conversations and then output a recall summary. Prior project lookup is expected for debugging, but cross-session memory or conversation access without consent or redaction is broader than the stated purpose requires.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789112194552}}}}}